### Goal Model Decomposition

#### Goals

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1 | Fulfill Resource Request | # | Perform | OR | The mission requires fulfilling multiple resource requests, which can be handled independently in parallel. |
| G2 | Resource Request X | ; | Perform | AND | Each resource request involves both collection and delivery phases, which must both succeed. |
| G2.1 | Collect Resource X | - | Perform | AND | Part of G2, must be completed before delivery. |
| G2.2 | Deliver Resource X | - | Perform | AND | Part of G2, must be completed after collection. |

#### Tasks

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT1 | Collect from Storage X | AND | Storage X | 1 | Single robot collects resource X. |
| AT2 | Deliver to Location X | AND | Delivery Location X | 1 | Single robot delivers resource X after collection. |

### Logical Relationships

1. **G1 -> G2, G3, ... [OR, Parallel]**
   - Justification: Multiple resource requests can be handled independently and in parallel to reduce mission time.

2. **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [AND, Sequential]**
   - Justification: Each resource request requires both collection and delivery phases, which must be completed sequentially.

3. **G2.1 -> AT1 [AND]**
   - Justification: The collection task must be performed to fulfill the collection phase.

4. **G2.2 -> AT2 [AND]**
   - Justification: The delivery task must be performed to fulfill the delivery phase.

This goal model effectively decomposes the mission into manageable subtasks, allowing for efficient parallel execution of independent resource requests while ensuring each request is fully processed through sequential collection and delivery phases.
